Rule 1 (input to atleast_1d must be a tensor or a tuple/list of tensors; if it's a list/tuple, all elements must be tensors)
{v_1 : tensor ⊎ list(tensor) ⊎ tuple(tensor)} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 then true else false
>>
Rule 2 (if input to atleast_1d is a tuple/list of tensors, at least one tensor should be present)
{v_1 : list(tensor) ⊎ tuple(tensor)} |= v_1.len > 0
>>
Rule 3 (if input is a tensor, the dtype must be a valid tensor dtype, and dimensions should be at least 0)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
